From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: phy: qcom: edp: end v8 power-on with the values UEFI leaves

Christian Cortner (A16 owner) reported on Bjorn Andersson's "phy: qcom:
edp: update v8 power-on programming sequence" (v1, 2026-06-22; rc5
0002/0003 here), Message-ID
<179346367993.44447.8683103034067826560.x2e-share-edp@gmail.com>, that
the A16's UEFI ends eDP PHY power-on with five registers set differently
from the series, and that writing the UEFI values at the end of
power-on made every 4-lane HBR2 link train cleanly:

  DP_PHY_CFG_1             0x2f -> 0x0f
  DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL  0x05 -> 0x00
  TXn_RESET_TSYNC_EN       0x0a -> 0x03 (tx0 and tx1)
  DP_PHY_TSYNC_OVRD        0x3e -> 0x10
  DP_PHY_CFG after DCC     0x09 -> 0x19

Write them after a successful DCC calibration in
qcom_edp_finish_power_on_v8(). Nothing else changes; ldo_config stays
at the series' 0xd0. Which of the five matters is not known.

Measured on the A16, natural link training only (failed attempts are
recovered by msm-dp-edp-link-training-retry):
  gen 89 (a16-7.4 + this):  0 of 500 fb0 blank/unblank enables and
                            0 of 162 boots with a failed attempt
  gen 85 (a16-7.4 without): 30 of 400 enables, 8 of 61 boots
  gen 80 (a16-7.3-bridge):  6 of 100 enables, 7 of 106 boots
All links ended at HBR2 x4. Beads 9bu (test), c34 (carry, approved
2026-11-03).

Carried until Bjorn's next revision of the series; drop it then if the
revision programs these values, or re-test.
Assisted-by: LLM
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
@@ -1592,7 +1592,23 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return qcom_edp_run_dcc_calibration(edp);
+	ret = qcom_edp_run_dcc_calibration(edp);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * End power-on with the five values the A16's UEFI leaves (Christian
+	 * Cortner's report on the v8 power-on series); carried until the
+	 * series' next revision.
+	 */
+	writel(0x0f, edp->edp + DP_PHY_CFG_1);
+	writel(0x00, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL);
+	writel(0x03, edp->tx0 + TXn_RESET_TSYNC_EN);
+	writel(0x03, edp->tx1 + TXn_RESET_TSYNC_EN);
+	writel(0x10, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TSYNC_OVRD);
+	writel(0x19, edp->edp + DP_PHY_CFG);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int qcom_edp_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
